    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks()` returns a list of extmarks of type `vim.api.keyset.get_extmark_item`. This cannot be passed in directly to `vim.pos.extmark()`, and requires some finagling:\n\n```lua\nlocal extmarks = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(...)\nlocal extmark = extmarks[index]\nlocal pos = vim.pos.extmark(0, extmark[2], extmark[3])\n```\n\nThe same problem applies to `vim.range`:\n\n```lua\nlocal extmarks = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(..., { details = true })\nlocal extmark = extmarks[index]\nlocal range = vim.pos.extmark(0, extmark[2], extmark[3], extmark[4].end_row, extmark[4].end_col)\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nOverload `vim.pos.extmark({buf}, {row}, {col})` to have a `vim.pos.extmark({buf}, {extmark})` form:\n\n```lua\nlocal extmarks = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(...)\nlocal pos = vim.pos.extmark(0, extmarks[index])\n```\n\nAdditionally, overload `vim.range.extmark({buf}, {start_row}, {start_col}, {end_row}, {end_col})` to have a `vim.range.extmark({buf}, {extmark})` form:\n\n```lua\nlocal extmarks = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(..., { details = true })\nlocal range = vim.range.extmark(0, extmarks[index])\n```\n\n(If this is wanted I can implement this myself)",
    "closed_at": null,
