            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "When adding the overload for `vim.pos.cursor`, I considered adding this, but I didn't think it would be very practical. \n\nAn extmark is ofte a visual representation of some other underlying data type, such as an inlay hint or code lens. Because of this, even though we use `set_extmark` extensively, we rarely use `get_extmark`.\n\nWe can try it out in our current codebase, which will help us determine if it actually brings any real practical value.",
