            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> We can try it out in our current codebase, which will help us determine if it actually brings any real practical value.\n\nThe interesting thing about this is that `vim.{pos,range}.extmark()` itself is currently completely unused in Nvim core. Presumably all potential uses of it have not been refactored yet.\n\n> An extmark is ofte a visual representation of some other underlying data type, such as an inlay hint or code lens. Because of this, even though we use `set_extmark` extensively, we rarely use `get_extmark`.\n\nI think `nvim_buf_set_extmark()` is more common in Nvim core, while `nvim_buf_get_extmarks()` is more typically used in configs/plugins (that's where it came up for me).",
